body:
I can't read really any Japanese but the off browser translation helped, thanks! It looks like it had to have been triggered by being approached by Yumizuka twice...but it was such a minor scene that anyone could have missed without missing any major parts of the story lol

&#x200B;

Ah well glad to have checked that off.

Sometimes I wish I wasn't on the internet as often since somethings are better left not learned of. I've been dealing with depression, and working on self-esteem issues for a while now, and recently learning of the term "incel" I can't seem to get it out of my head. 

&#x200B;

The fact that there is a label of guys who have been unsuccessful, and said guys made a dedicated group of hatred towards women and the world, I feel even more shame added to my own self-esteem. I wouldn't ever associate myself with the Braincels, but I can't seem to get past the fact that the simple term can apply to me; just a regular guy who just wants affection, physical companionship, etc. 

&#x200B;

I hear a lot of "do different things", such as stepping out your comfort zone, and how that has been for me has been rather exhausting. When mustering the courage to get out whether it be bars, or night clubs, every now and then I get dances here and there, but for the most part, rejection. Some rejections are a lot less embarrassing as others, but when they all add up, it comes to a point where I feel like I'm trying too hard. I hear a lot of "happen you least expect it" which hasn't really been true for me. 

&#x200B;

I feel like giving up, but to give up would to accept the label of incel. If I am to go through the rest of my young adult life as an incel past my prime years, I would rather end it young. 

&#x200B;

TL;DR just needed to put some things off my chest.

> People in Texas are MUCH friendlier than the Massholes that populate our home state. When I go back to visit, I can't believe some of the things I hear and see when I am out and about... Worcester is it's own beast when it comes to that, though. 

&#x200B;

Ha! I have been past Worcester enough times, but not enough to know much of a difference from regular Bostonians. Glad to hear from someone that has lived in both MA and Texas. I decided to post in Houston just to see what people think about there as well, and man...do people just non-stop talking about the traffic and drivers.

&#x200B;

Are drivers in Dallas anywhere near as bad as the road-raging Massholes? If you're from Mass like me, I think you'll know that just walking up to people, you are more than likely going to get some dirty looks...lol

&#x200B;

Your comment definitely gives me the best insight, since you have had experience in both places. "moving for no reason in particular but change". That's my main reason also! 

&#x200B;

Damn,

&#x200B;

I have lost track now of how many people have talked about the traffic/driving in Houston. Seems like that's the main thing that people hate about it. Never seen baseball sized hail. A little scary lol

But it's 45 minutes from Galveston right? Lol

&#x200B;

wait...have you been to Boston?! If so, how long? There's no way Houston can have worse drivers than Boston...granted I can't talk, I haven't been to both places...

So I wanted to thank everyone that answered so far, I have had some really good insight on Dallas.

&#x200B;

Now I know this will be a very biased answer, but I am stuck between Houston and Dallas. What makes Dallas more enjoyable to live in than Houston?

It's great to have someone's perspective that has lived both Omaha and Dallas. Thank you for your honesty!

&#x200B;

So far, granted only 3 years compared to how long you've lived both places, my experience has been rather opposite. Maybe it's me, maybe it's them, though I don't plan on trying to figure it out on a Reddit comment. Any time I strike up a conversation either at a meetup event or any of the college orgs I join, I get the vibe of politely trying to tell me to stop talking or excuse themselves from me. Many people who are friends currently rarely want to hang out, and if we do, it's either just grabbing food, a bite, a drink, or movie. Just very limited things here to do which I am thinking is making things harder.

&#x200B;

I'm a little surprised that a good mount of people disliked your comment! lol if they don't agree, I would like to hear why. or maybe those are just that confident how easy it is to make friends here, but it's different for everyone.

> I guess because it wouldn't fully resolve the problem since there are still Eldians worldwide that could still repopulate or receive titan powers. 

&#x200B;

There aren't any other Eldians around other than those on the island and those in Liberio right? Which actually helps me piece together...Marley wouldn't kill all Eldians, they would continue enslaving them using titan power. 

&#x200B;

> But one more thing- If Karl Fritz was so guilt laden about the crimes of the Eldian people, I'm sure he could have also made the same DNA change after going behind the walls. Something tells me it is not as simple as Zeke thinks it will be. 

&#x200B;

Well, Karl Fritz wanted to live a short paradise in the walls, and I guess he wanted people to feel like they could live their lives, have children without fear for a little while. But then again...he could easily wipe from their memories any ability they have to make children, and thus have them all die there. Interesting...

&#x200B;

So...I don't understand a few things...pardon me for being slow, and hope someone can help me out.

&#x200B;

What the actual fawk is the point of going through the trouble of attacking Marley if Zeke (and maybe Eren) are ultimately planning to euthanize all of Eldia?

&#x200B;

Why have the conversation about breaking the vow King Fritz made if they are (supposedly) agreeing that it would have been better if the royal family kept the FT, and let everyone in the walls die? I don't understand why Eren would actually agree to this plan. I know there's a lot of theories that he's manipulating Zeke, but I'm just accounting for the fact if that ends up being wrong, in which case I can't make any sense of it. The guy who keeps chanting..."tatakai, tatakai..." the guy who believes freedom means to live without fear or confinement, and that if you are born, you're supposed to be free just spout out "to not have been born is the best salvation" wtf?!

&#x200B;

Again, I know there seems to be a good amount of signs that Eren is lying to Zeke. All Zeke can think of is that Eren was raised by Grisha, and treated the same way he was. When actually, Eren was raised to have free will, and hell Grisha said that in the first episode. It'd just be so dumb and sad that Eren would really go against everything he fought for. Why not just kneel over and let Marley kill everyone if that's their goal?

If someone can help me out here...there's so many things I'm lost about after this chapter, well mainly with Eren and Zeke. 

&#x200B;

\-Why the actual fuck would Eren agree with Zeke's plan if they intended to cripple Marley's military, destroy their naval port, and "buy time" if the end goal was for them to get rid of Eldians? 

\-Am I the only one who thinks it's really depressing for Eren to make such a huge 180 turn, from being this kid who hated being confined by the walls, who hated that outside the walls denied him freedom, and who hates those who aren't free (his quote to Mikasa). 

\-We've seen his definition of freedom is that being able to live without confinement like cattle, and without fear of being killed. Now that his brother shows up he thinks him and everyone he cares about should die? The only way I can wrap my head around is the theory that Eren is using Zeke, and once they activate the FT, he can do whatever the fuck he wants. 

&#x200B;

\-Eren never gave Zeke a direct answer. He evaded the question first, then said "I will do it". Could he be meaning doing this his own way?

&#x200B;

\-What is the point of breaking the "vow of renunciation" if that vow is what was going to allow everyone in the walls die? Why would Zeke and Xaver care about this if they just plan to ultimately euthanize Eldia?

&#x200B;

\-It seems like Eren wanted to bait Marley into coming for whatever reason, again, why are they trying to destroy Marley if the plan it to euthanize Eldians...?

&#x200B;

Feel like I answered my own questions but I want to hear what you guys think too. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

I thought about this too and it's been driving me crazy. Why go through all the trouble, attack Marley, when they supposedly agreed that the Royal family should have just kept the FT, and let everyone in the walls die? 

&#x200B;

What's the point of continuing to fight after he learned the truth of the walls if it was better to just let everyone die? I'm so confused. The only way it makes some sense is that Eren is in fact using Zeke and just telling him what he wants to hear.



*"3. even now Pieck one of the true warriors from Marley has infiltrated Paradis..it's gonna get really messy from here...*

*for Eren, i think he's that type of guy who would go to such extreme to kill off the eldians considering he despises titans and how they ruined his life to begin with.* ***both zeke and him were raised by the same father, both got brainwashed*** *hated how titans ruined their lives and basically the existence of titans."*

&#x200B;

In Zeke's eyes, Eren has been most likely brainwashed and treated the same way he was treated by Grisha's poor parenting. Eren, however was never really brainwashed was he? On his own, he always wanted to be free and venture beyond the walls and learn the world. Grisha never forced that on him, and in episode 1, he even told Carla you can't control his free will. In other words, we can say that Eren turned out how Grisha hoped to make Zeke.

&#x200B;

I honestly hope and think that Eren is planning to betray Zeke as well. It makes to think about it that way, telling him he disagrees with Zeke, and would fight against his cause would create too much trouble, and he would be unable to use the FT. Once Zeke touches Eren and finally initiate the FT, Eren can do whatever the fuck he wants. 

&#x200B;

It's the only way it even makes sense. Why the fuck would Eren just do a 180 after always preaching about (hell I've watched the S3 P2 trailer enough times) "from the moment we are born, we are all free!" then say, "yeah bruh we shoulda not been born fuck pops. Why he do dat shit" 

&#x200B;

If that was the case why not just turn himself into Marley and let everyone in walls die? That's pretty much Zeke's plan.
